sequenceDiagram
    participant GH as GitHub (pull_request paths / workflow_dispatch)
    participant Job as benchmark job<br/>ubuntu-latest
    participant JC as jcstress job<br/>ubuntu-latest
    participant STS as AWS STS
    participant CLI as baas CLI<br/>(reactor build)
    participant AWS as Deployment

    GH->>Job: trigger (one at a time per ref, never cancelled mid-run)
    GH->>JC: same trigger, the two jobs run in parallel, each with its own instance
    Job->>Job: mvn clean package -DskipTests
    Job->>STS: AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity(vars.OPERATOR_ROLE_ARN, 9000 s)
    STS-->>Job: operator credentials in the environment (no profile)
    Job->>CLI: config sync --deployment vars.CORE_STACK_NAME
    Note over Job,CLI: sync finds the deployment's region from its bucket and stores it,<br/>so the job follows the deployment whatever vars.AWS_REGION says
    CLI->>AWS: DescribeStacks
    Job->>CLI: run jmh-with-async --detach --format json --timeout 7200 --watchdog-margin 300<br/>--project <repo> --tag branch --tag commit --tag exclude_from_results=true<br/>--runner-jar target/benchmark-runner.jar --benchmark-jar fake-jmh-benchmarks.jar<br/>-- Incrementing_Synchronized -f 1 -wi 1 -i 1 --async-…
    CLI->>AWS: upload, launch, confirm -- NO poll (see baas-run.mmd, opt --detach)
    CLI-->>Job: one JSON object on stdout, status launched, exit 0 -- the CLI is gone
    Job->>Job: GITHUB_OUTPUT job_id, result_path, project -- asserts status launched
    loop every 15 s until a terminal status or vanished, at most timeout + margin + 15 s
        Job->>CLI: jobs show <id> --format json (a failed lookup is retried)
        CLI->>AWS: GetItem + DescribeInstances
        CLI-->>Job: status
        Note over CLI,AWS: meanwhile the instance ends the job alone -- completed or failed:N,<br/>or timed-out from its watchdog
    end
    Job->>Job: GITHUB_OUTPUT job_status, the last status read
    Job->>CLI: results --job-id <id> --format json
    Note over Job: asserts imageVersion, instanceType, project, branch, commit, source=ci
    Job->>CLI: results --project <repo> --best-per commit --format json
    Note over Job: asserts the excluded job is absent
    Job->>CLI: results --project <repo> --show-excluded --format json
    Note over Job: asserts it is present
    Job->>CLI: download <run_id> -o ./artifacts
    Note over Job: asserts environment.json, jmh-result.json, no legacy run-status object, output, flamegraph, JFR, and the followed job_status reads completed
    opt failure and a result_path was reported
        Job->>CLI: download <result_path> -o ./failed (by PATH: a failed job has no index entry)
        Job->>Job: print cloud-init-output.log
    end
    Job->>GH: upload ./artifacts
    Note over JC,CLI: same build, federation and config sync as the benchmark job
    JC->>CLI: run jcstress --format json --project <repo><br/>--tag branch --tag commit --tag exclude_from_results=true<br/>--runner-jar target/benchmark-runner.jar --benchmark-jar fake-stress-tests.jar<br/>-- --mode sanity
    CLI->>AWS: upload, launch, poll (see baas-run.mmd)
    CLI-->>JC: one JSON object on stdout
    Note over JC: asserts the summary jobStatus reads completed
    JC->>CLI: results --job-id <id> --format json
    Note over JC: asserts exactly one row, benchmarkType jcstress, a (jcstress) name and the job's tags,<br/>never pass or fail counts, since the fixture's forbidden test races
    JC->>CLI: download <run_id> -o ./artifacts
    Note over JC: asserts environment.json and jcstress-output.txt
    JC->>GH: upload ./artifacts
